{
  "name": "derpfs",
  "description": "derpfs is an experimental FUSE-based filesystem implementation that leverages memory-mapped I/O to manage on-disk data structures within a linear address space. It defines a custom disk layout featuring superblocks, bitmap-based block allocation, and hierarchical entity metadata, while intentionally incorporating a background fault-injection thread to simulate system instability.",
